\par \pard\plain \s0\sl360\slmult1\widctlpar\sb0\sa240\ltrpar\hyphpar0\kerning0\cf1\rtlch\af13\afs22\alang1025\ltrch\hich\af8\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af11\langfe1033\loch\f8\fs24\lang1033\sl276\slmult1\keep\sb0\sa160{\cf1\fs24
Fig. 4. Sensitivity to specified differential-censoring models. (A) The headline coefficient reaches zero when displacement changes by 0.185 pH units per predictor standard deviation. (B) For the two proxies with effects in the threatening direction, required displacement exceeds available headroom under an assumed pH 0 floor. This floor is a modeling assumption, not a universal physical boundary; these calculations do not exclude unmeasured censoring mechanisms. Orange bars show required depth and grey bars headroom to the assumed floor.}
